# `node_modules` alone matches only the context root: dockerignore patterns are
# matched against the whole relative path, and a bare name does not match at
# depth. `packages/socket/node_modules` was therefore copied into the image —
# its dev-only eslint and typescript links included — and a pnpm workspace
# symlink inside it (`@evimed/domain -> ../../../domain`) silently redirected a
# later COPY out of the package and into /opt/evimed/domain. The image worked
# through that accident. This pattern is the one that actually excludes them.
**/node_modules
node_modules
.git
apps/*/node_modules
apps/desktop/dist
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/binaries
.openscience-web-data
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
secrets
**/secrets
deploy/web/release-manifest.json

# Probe artefacts, not build inputs. A run leaves a workspace of fetched
# sources here — sometimes root-owned, since the probe runs in a container —
# and the build sender reads the whole context, so one unreadable file aborts
# the image with a permission error that names a file nothing in the image
# wants.
evals/capability-audit/results/tool-probe-workspace
evals/capability-audit/tool-probe-workspace
evals/**/results/runs
